// @run
// @log a
// @log 3
// @hint redundant type annotation: `a` is inferred as `string` — remove it to lean on inference
// THE REGRESSION #1481 SHIPPED, AND THE SHAPE THE CORPUS COULD NOT SUPPLY.
//
// `T | string` at `T := string` substitutes to a union whose two members are the SAME type.
// The annotation path folds that — `nameToTy("string|string")` collapses to plain `string`,
// which is also why the SOURCE spelling `const v: string | string` compiles and runs.
// `substTyDeep` does NOT fold it: it rebuilds the union member-wise and stops.
//
// #1481 handed the substituted type over as the instance's return type, so the binding was
// recorded as a UNION BOX while the instance returns a bare `(ref $str)`: `vl check
// --codegen` rc 0 and `vl run` "expected (ref null $type), found (ref $type)". The first
// line below ran correctly before #1481 and was broken by it.
//
// TWO THINGS LET IT THROUGH, both worth naming. The dual-run that licensed the hand-over
// compared RENDERS and filed the union cells under "differs only nominally" — but for a
// union the recorded TYPE is what picks the box, so a differing render is not cosmetic
// there. And the corpus A/B read 0 of 2,021, because no corpus program has a generic whose
// return union COLLAPSES under its binding — the same blindness this branch has now hit
// four times, and the reason the fix ships with a fixture rather than a measurement.
//
// THE HINT ABOVE IS THE FIX WORKING. `substTyDeep` now folds a degenerate union the way
// `nameToTy` does, so the checker resolves this call as plain `string` and correctly reports
// the annotation as redundant. Before the fold it saw a two-member union and said nothing —
// the annotation looked load-bearing because the type was wrong. The hint is declared rather
// than removed so that a regression in the fold shows up as a MISSING hint here.
//
// The INFERRED binding over the same collapse is a SEPARATE and older defect — it is
// check-clean invalid wasm on master, before #1481 and after this fix alike, and is filed at
// B9 in docs/internals/destringify-types-program.md. It is deliberately not exercised here:
// this file pins the regression and its control, not that.
function f<T>(v: T): T | string {
  v
}

// ANNOTATED binding over a COLLAPSING union — correct before #1481, broken by it, restored.
const a: string = f("a")
print(a)

// The control the exclusion must not disturb: arms that stay DISTINCT.
const c = f(3)
if c is i32 { print(c) }
